Description: The `responses.build` package provides a workflow to harmonise physiological response-curve data - leaf gas exchange, hydraulic vulnerability, and fluorescence response curves - from diverse sources into a documented, relational structure. It is a fork of `traits.build` (Wenk et al, 2024, <doi:10.1016/j.ecoinf.2024.102773>, <https://github.com/traitecoevo/traits.build>), which harmonises single-valued trait data; this package extends the same data model to measurements that form curves, where a response is measured across a driver gradient and the individual points belong to an identifiable curve. It was built to support AusFizz (<https://github.com/traitecoevo/ausfizz>). For the shared data model and workflow concepts see <https://traitecoevo.github.io/traits.build-book/>.
BugReports: https://github.com/traitecoevo/responses.build/issues
